build123d is a Python parametric boundary representation (BREP) CAD
modeling framework for 2D and 3D CAD, built on the OpenCascade
geometric kernel (through the OCP bindings).  Models are written as
Python code in a builder style (BuildPart, BuildSketch, BuildLine
context managers) or an algebra style, and can be imported from and
exported to STEP, STL, 3MF, glTF, BREP, DXF and SVG.
